#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hearth's AI hub (shell/services/Ai.qml, README "AI").

One place for every model the desktop uses: local servers (Ollama,
llama.cpp's llama-server in router mode, Magnitude, systemd user units that
serve one model such as inkling-2-mini.service), models other apps keep in
graphics memory (found by the model files they have open), every model
installed anywhere (helpers/hearth_ai_models.py: Hugging Face cache, model
folders, LM Studio, ComfyUI, Piper...) sorted by category, and coding-agent
CLIs (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini). It loads and unloads models, installs
and deletes them, reports GPU load and VRAM per GPU, per process and per
model, and runs the assistant (voice and Spotlight's "Ask") with tools.

Graphics memory is managed (class Arbiter): a model that hasn't used the
GPU for a while unloads (later for models that take long to load), and
when the card fills up the models idle longest and quickest to load again
are evicted first, so a new request finds room. `hearth-ai --make-room
UNIT|BYTES` does the same on demand (model units call it in ExecStartPre).

JSON lines on stdin/stdout, so the shell never waits:

  {"cmd": "refresh"}                      -> {"type": "state", ...}
  {"cmd": "watch", "on": true}            poll every 2 s while a UI shows it
  {"cmd": "load"|"unload", "provider": "ollama", "model": "qwen3.5:4b"}
  {"cmd": "unloadAll"}
  {"cmd": "pull", "provider": "ollama", "model": "..."}   -> {"type": "pull", ...}
  {"cmd": "delete", "provider": "ollama", "model": "..."}
  {"cmd": "server", "provider": "llamacpp", "on": true}   (systemd user unit)
  {"cmd": "ask", "id": 3, "feature": "assistant", "text": "...", "context": {...}}
      -> {"type": "tool", "id": 3, "call": 1, "name": "launch_app", "args": {...}}
      -> {"type": "approve", "id": 3, "call": 2, "kind": "command"|"computer", "title": ..., "detail": ...}
         (the shell shows Allow/Deny and answers toolResult with "allow" or "deny";
         {"type": "approved", ...} follows when the question is gone)
         (the shell runs it and answers {"cmd": "toolResult", "id": 3, "call": 1, "result": "..."})
      -> {"type": "reply", "id": 3, "text": "...", "done": true}
  {"cmd": "cancel", "id": 3}
  {"cmd": "catalog", "category": "tts", "query": ""}  -> {"type": "catalog", ...}
  {"cmd": "install", "provider": "hf"|"ollama"|"magnitude"|"lmstudio"|"runtime:localai:<port>", "model": "..."}
      -> {"type": "pull", ...}
  {"cmd": "remove", "key": "<installed key>"}          (provider delete, or files to the trash)
  {"cmd": "loadKey"|"unloadKey", "key": "<installed or loaded key>"}
  {"cmd": "pin", "key": "...", "on": true}              never unload it automatically

Settings come from settings.json `ai` (Settings > AI). Cloud CLIs are used
only when `ai.allowCloud` is on.

Apps get the same models through an OpenAI-compatible server on 127.0.0.1
(class ApiServer, README "AI" > Apps): its address and token are in
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hearth/ai-api.json while this runs.
"""

